        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "a. The parties agree that the Human Resource Services Division Personnel Policies and Agency Procedures relating to their implementation are without effect upon the Agency or members of the bargaining units.",
            "block_bbox": [
                104,
                134,
                1118,
                209
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    104.0,
                    134.0
                ],
                [
                    1118.0,
                    134.0
                ],
                [
                    1118.0,
                    209.0
                ],
                [
                    104.0,
                    209.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "b. Other policies, procedures, and rules of the Agency which directly relate to mandatory subjects of bargaining as defined by statute and which affect bargaining unit members on the day this Agreement becomes effective shall be continued, unless modified or deleted elsewhere in this Agreement. Should the Agency wish to change such a policy, procedure, or rule, or to issue a new one, notice will be given to the Union. If the Union believes the policy, procedure, or rule to be unreasonable, then within seven (7) days of the date upon which the Union knows, or by reasonable diligence should have known, of the subject action, the Union shall request that the Agency meet to discuss the issue.",
            "block_bbox": [
                103,
                210,
                1119,
                411
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
